# November 21, 2026: Troy and Lansingburgh (region troy, drawn at random by tools/choose.py --state ny), the ground the
# Atlas had not yet covered there: Oakwood Cemetery and its two chapels (a full entry replacing the thin lm- pin), the
# downtown buildings still missing (the county courthouse, St. John's Episcopal Church, the Rice Building, the Paine
# Mansion, the National State Bank, the house at 1819 Fifth Avenue, the Pumpkin House), the Northern River Street
# collar-factory block, Register houses away from downtown (Glenwood, the Henry Koon House, the Powers Home), the former
# St. Barnabas Episcopal Church, the Eglise Saint Jean Baptiste marker, and just over the line in North Greenbush the
# Little Red Schoolhouse. Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py), HMdb marker pages,
# the Oakwood Cemetery Association's pages, the Episcopal Diocese of Albany's page for St. John's, historypointer.com
# for Register addresses, the Lansingburgh Historical Society, the North Greenbush town historian's column and a 2020
# radio-station news item, all read with tools/page.py.
